    width*leftPct/100; the dot colour = FSMStateColor.tint (the reused
    getStateColor port); the web <button> tick -> a plain SwiftUI Button with a
    .help() tooltip + accessibilityLabel/Value; selection grows the dot + a
    contrast ring. Shared @/components/ui -> TSButton / TSQueryError / TSSkeleton;
    tokens Color.TS / Font.TS / TSSpacing / TSRadius (compiled against the REAL
    DesignTokens + component library in [3]/[4]).
  Adapter -> StateTimelineProjection is a 1:1 port of the web useMemo:
    endTs=(anchor ?? now); startTs=endTs-windowMinutes*60s; span=(endTs-startTs)||1;
    sort transitions by ts asc (id tie-break for determinism); leftPct=
    ((ts-startTs)/span)*100; start/end anchors. presetLabel + formatRelative are
    byte-faithful value-type ports (verified against their web thresholds in [6]).
  States (all render) -> empty (web ticks.length===0): "No transitions in window",
    and when a lastTransition exists outside the window, "· Last transition {rel}"
